      <div class="kpi-label">Discount-Rating Corr.</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Weak negative relationship</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> The catalog is healthy — 3 in 4 products (75.8%) are rated 4.0 or above. However, the average discount of 47.7% is aggressive, and the weak negative correlation (r = −0.16) between discount depth and rating suggests that deeper discounts do <em>not</em> improve customer satisfaction. Heavy promotions may be eroding margin without lifting perceived quality.
